15	//   already the newest shape, so there is no older state to migrate. Replaying
16	//   history onto a fresh install is not merely wasted work — a record assumes the
17	//   shapes ITS ERA produced, and an empty repo is not one of them, so the replay is
18	//   a hazard. The install fetches no records and stamps the LATEST version directly;
19	//   migrations exist for repos installed at an older one.
20	//
21	// Everything else is the pack flow's: same vendor set, same self-test gate, same
22	// terminals. What differs is only where it starts.
23	//
24	// AN INSTALL IS NOT AN UPDATE IN DISGUISE. A pack the repo already has a version for
25	// is refused rather than reinstalled: reinstalling would stamp the newest version
26	// while skipping every record between, which is exactly how a member ends up
27	// claiming a state it was never migrated into.
